A||N||9||DaRkLoRD||got stranded, yelled at, and then robbed......||||8||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||11-04-2000||01:29 AM||||I had the (mis)fortune of taking the bus home for the weekend, as the friend whom I usually get a ride with, was busy this weekend and wasn't going home.<BR>I decided I'd take the bus from the airport.. so I asked another friend if he could drive me there on friday afternoon.<BR>I needed to be there at 5pm, but what he didn't tell me is that he was in class until 4:30! So I was getting a bit anxious.. anyway, we made it there ok and I found someone and asked where the bus terminal was. she said it was downstairs and to the left.. ok, makes sense. I go down... nothing. so I go to another desk and ask, and this old lady says THERE IS NO BUS.... I'm like "uhh.. yeah there is, I've taken it before.. just not from the airport!" so she starts telling me some story about how she took the bus one time and it cost her $60.. I'm looking at my watch because it's getting really late, and finally I thank her for telling me where the departures section was, and I go there. Luckily, that's where I was supposed to be. I find out where the bus is going to arrive, and I wait outside. and waited.. and waited.. the bus was 40 minutes late. Anyway, as I'm waiting, I meet this guy who lives 10 mins away from my college, and his home town is 30 mins away from where I'm from. so we're talking, etc. and we get on the bus when it finally arrives. At one of the stops, we get out to get some slices of pizza, cause we're hungry.. when we're about to pay, I look outside and see the bus driving off, without us.<BR>So there we were, stuck in some town, with none of our luggage, etc.. all I had was my wallet. (and adam, the guy I was with, didn't even have that.. he left it in his backpack.. which was now en route to the next city.....)<BR>Anyway, luckily the girl at the pizza place was kind enough to call ahead to the next stop and have the bus wait.. if we could get there in time! We lucked out, a taxi had just pulled into the parking lot, and he said he could take us to the next stop. so, we jumped in the cab and followed the bus.. and we caught up to it at the next stop. So, it seemed that everything was good. until we got back on, and discovered that someone had gone through our things and stolen some stuff, including my CD player....<BR>later on, I was having a conversation with the guy next to me, and some old bitchy lady sitting 3 rows up was eavesdropping.. but she kept butting into the conversation, and was extremely rude.. not only did she tell me that I was in the wrong college program (I'm interested in biomedical technology, and I'm currently studying electro-mechanical engineering, she said that I should be in kineisology instead) but she also said what I was talking about was total BS (I was telling the guy about a type of cancer treatment that has been around for a while but is being blocked by the AMA)<BR>I also commented that as soon as a cure for cancer is made readily available, the cancer society's funding is going to disappear, so financially it would be in their best interest for a cure to remain unavailable.. this lady took that to mean I was accusing the cancer society of fraud, and she said I should go to Interpol.... but she said it in a very sarcastic way, and it was obvious she was intending to be offensive. call me weird, but if she didn't like what I was saying (in a private conversation) that's not my fault, she shouldn't have been listening in anyway.<P>overall, it's been quite an interesting night.. and if it weren't for my cd player being stolen and being yelled at by this old lady.. it would have been fun.<P>Sorry for the long post.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||8
Z||000001||onfire||11-04-2000||02:32 AM||||Could have been worse. I few months ago my friends Fiero was stolen.Its an 86(i think) with 17" wheels red and real nice. While he was at AM-PM, buying a soda.The car was recovered about 8 days later, but the police didn't check the vin#. So they auctioned it off, for $1050.00.The guy who bought it went to get it liscensed found out it was stolen.So he had to give the car back.My friend finally got it back from the police almost two months later.And the only thing missing was the stereo.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.on_fire/files/onfirepff.JPG">   <BR>  <A HREF="http://homestead.deja.com/user.on_fire/on_fire.html" TARGET=_blank><B>Check out my little waist of bandwidth onfire</B></A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ed||11-04-2000||11:28 AM||||I suppose anyone who uses the bus, subway or light rail has similar stories.  <P>We have the above ground light rail here in Sacramento. I'd ride it during midday to go to meetings in downtown Sacramento.  You certainly could meet some interesting people, including released cons from Folsom prison.   ||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||11-05-2000||02:23 AM||||Maybe its because its late, and Im on my new laptop (instead of my desktop that I usually use) and the writing is incredibly tiny, but I hope you were kidding about the cure for cancer thing...................||||reg||5
Z||000004||Raydar||11-05-2000||05:40 PM||||Steve, When I read the "robbed" header, I thought you were gonna tell us that you had been mugged. Admittedly, having your stuff stolen sucks, but it's good that it wasn't "up close and personal". As for the AMA thing, I wouldn't be surprised. Hope it's not true, though.<BR>Cynical? Maybe. <P>Raydar||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||11-05-2000||05:58 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>I hope you were kidding about the cure for cancer thing...................</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No, I'm not actually.. 2 years ago my grandmother was diagnosed with breast and lymphatic cancer.. so I started researching everything I could find about cancer, and found some very interesting things.. I need to do a lot more research before I'm ready to tell people my theories in any detail, but I'm currently going to school to learn how to build a device to work with my research findings.<P>I'm not a doctor, I'm an engineering student.. and because of this, a lot of people dismiss my ideas without even considering them. That's why I don't like talking about them in detail, unless I trust the person.<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 11-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||My7Fieros||11-07-2000||12:31 AM||||ehhh.......ok||||reg||5
Z||000007||DaRkLoRD||11-07-2000||12:48 AM||||if someone wants to hear my ideas because they're interested, that's cool.. but if they just want to hear them to laugh and ridicule me, that's not cool. so that's why I don't like to discuss my theories unless I know the person is genuinely interested.<P>case in point, in 1997 I told my dad about an idea I had for killing cancer cells with pulses of electricity (this was before I got really into the research) and he told me it wouldn't work.. 2 years later, the exact same idea was presented in a medical journal, and suddenly he thought it was great.. and he conveniently forgot I'd described the same thing 2 years before.... nice, eh?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||2
Z||000008||Raydar||11-07-2000||10:01 AM||||The easiest way to kill a good idea is to say "but that's not the way we do it". If nobody ever had a "conflicting" vision, or refused to buck the established way of thinking, we'd all still be worried about sailing off the edge of the world. <BR>In whatever you do, follow your instincts. If they turn out to be incorrect, at least you tried. If they turn out to be correct, who knows? <P>Something has been in the back of my mind for a while, now. <BR>Seems like about a year ago, I heard about some lab experiments that showed great promise in killing cancer cells. Seems like there were like two amino acids or other genetic components that caused the production of cancer cells, that could be easily isolated and counteracted. Have you heard anything else about this?<P>Raydar<P><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 11-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||11-07-2000||12:42 PM||||I believe so, but my education background is electrical as opposed to biological, so I've been working at this from an engineering angle.. but anyway, there are many new ideas, which haven't yet reached the public, even though most of them were proven years ago.. how many more people need to die before the people in charge realize saving lives is more important than any other goals ($$$?) they have. This goes for all branches of medicine. my grandfather died of lung cancer when I was younger, and just a few years ago we lost several family friends within a period of 2 months. We think my grandmother is ok, but she's still having tests done. chemo etc does work, but it has a lot of side effects, and many people still do die. I'm simply saying there are better treatments in existance, but they're not being made available.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
